# Plasma Login Manager config for @DISTRO_NAME@'s LIVE VIEW — plan/34 §5.
#
# NOT config/rootfs. Everything under config/rootfs/etc goes into the lower via
# install_rootfs_overlay, which ships inside the read-only EROFS on every profile's build —
# including an installed disk's. This file is the live user's autologin, and the live user
# leaves the root image entirely (plan/34 §5): stage 40 renders THIS template by hand, straight
# into the /etc overlay's upper on $TARGET/var, which only a live boot of this image (this
# medium, desktop.img, console.img) ever merges over the lower. An installed disk gets a fresh
# /var and never receives it.
#
# A drop-in, not a replacement config: kde-plasma/plasma-login-manager's ebuild installs its
# own /etc/plasmalogin.conf.d/01gentoo.conf (it blanks InputMethod to drop the
# qtvirtualkeyboard default) — into the LOWER, same as always, since that file is the package's
# own and never touches the live user. The 10- prefix sorts after it, so both apply once the
# overlay merges upper and lower into one directory listing.
#
# PLM is a fork of SDDM and keeps its config syntax, so [Autologin] User/Session/Relogin carry
# over unchanged. CONFIRMED against plasma-login-manager 6.6.6's own Configuration.h: the
# section is [Autologin], the keys are User/Session/Relogin, and Session names a file in
# .../wayland-sessions with the ".desktop" appended for you, so "plasma" is right.
#
# THE FILE BEING CORRECT IS NOT ENOUGH, and this is the trap to know about before editing it:
# PLM only reads this directory when its newest mtime beats a zero-initialised "already loaded"
# stamp, so every inode in the image needs a non-zero mtime or nothing here is ever parsed and
# the greeter comes up with no error logged anywhere. Stage 60 stamps SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH into the
# EROFS for exactly this reason; it shipped as -T0 (the Unix epoch) through 0.3.0, and autologin
# was dead in every one of those images. This file no longer lives in the EROFS stage 60 stamps —
# it is a plain `render_template` write in stage 40, which always carries the build's real
# wall-clock time, never zero, so the trap does not apply here BY CONSTRUCTION. It still applies
# to var.img's mtimes in general; nothing in this file's own path should ever pass -T0 or
# `touch -d @0` to it. Stage 70 asserts autologin=yes so a regression cannot go unnoticed.
#
# Session names /usr/share/wayland-sessions/plasma.desktop, installed by
# kde-plasma/plasma-login-sessions[wayland]. Stage 40 asserts that file exists in the lower for
# exactly this reason. No [General] or [Wayland] compositor block belongs here: PLM drives kwin
# itself, which is why it RDEPENDs kwin[lock].
[Autologin]
User=@LIVE_USER@
Session=plasma
Relogin=false
